                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Mr John de Stok' was instituted to Twyford,
                        Bucks. in 1241 (Rot. Rob. Grosseteste, p. 359). A Mr John de Stok' bought
                        Royal MS. 8 A VIII at Hoxne Suffolk in 1246.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="12XX">s. xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_533">Sudbury, Suffolk.
                        Dominican convent. </orgName><p>'Hunc librum contulat [sic] magister
                        Iohannes de Stok' presbiter et rector ecclesiarum de Twyford et Hunede pro
                        salute anime sue et omnium parochianorum suorum deo et beate marie et
                        communitati fratrum predicatorum Sulbirie commorantium: qui fraudulenter
                        quocunque genere alienacionis a dicta communitate alienaverit vel scripturam
                        istam quocumque tempore maliciose preter suam conscientiam deleverit ipso
                        facto anathema est maranata, salvo tamen Iohanni de Hundene sacterdoti et
                        dicto I. si velit usu dicti libri suo dumtaxat perpetuo. Actum a. d. mo cco
                        lo sexto duodecimo Kal. marcii' (fol. 227v).</p><p>Inscr. erased at foot of
                        fol. 1r.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">s. xvi Parish church of Melburn, q. v.
